` command is used to send an HTTP GET request to the application running on `http://127.0.0.1:8080`. This is a common method for checking if a web server is responding.\n- **Exit Code Handling**: The script checks the exit code of `wget` after sending the request. If the exit code is `0`, it indicates that the application is healthy and the health check passes. Any other exit code results in a failure, with multiple failures indicating an unhealthy instance.\n\n### Companion Files Together\n\nSince this is a single file, there are no companion files to document together as one unit.", "vector": [-0.085224405, 0.007073853, -0.0065074484, -0.01471012, 0.04735022, -0.0021819158, -0.0029832418, 0.04743182, -0.06214563, -0.07533349, 0.062072344, 0.029779188, 0.012748665, -0.020008039, -0.009817621, 0.037915092, 0.056053184, 0.042419404, -0.05957503, 0.044678368, -0.039939485, 0.0005622602, -0.007190122, -0.03333595, -0.0036435085, -0.0017678839, 0.023254996, -0.03996743, -0.0015133214, -0.0412806, 0.008883795, 0.039120656, 0.006791559, 0.03127332, 0.029327534, -0.0018377982, 0.009620971, 0.0025581347, 0.07390224, -0.009495308, 0.019051142, 0.08087348, 0.014683438, 0.046701845, 0.0022786618, -0.100893475, -0.03618338, -0.052881833, 0.010595299, 0.001033308, -0.011249065, 0.05669277, -0.024683867, 0.057292987, 0.03112547, 0.026184967, -0.05135579, 0.0030180432, -0.038408447, 0.023939807, -0.015771458, -0.055490658, -0.004828739, 0.028035287, 0.021105716, 0.028633319, 0.037962567, -0.0311377, 0.015681203, 0.095061384, 0.03524986, -0.07384135, -0.02122707, -0.07124095, 0.14402679, 0.042715248, -0.003491784, 0.021820916, 0.04719829, 0.034088615, 0.036289845, 0.04227592, -0.075452626, -0.07480665, 0.07836153, 0.057051063, -0.042392697, -0.0630762, 0.041811608, -0.04635169, -0.050092667, 0.019604033, 0.022259977, 0.027210262, 0.02707424, -0.031558324, -0.0131687345, 0.03970618, -0.021367857, -0.036970925, 0.007978078, -0.034997735, 0.053727638, 0.0070738615, 0.015231556, 0.0111